"id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T04:49:12Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T04:58:16Z","body":"Replacing the scene root in the open scene (the scene being edited) requires some additional operations, mainly done by `EditorNode::set_edited_scene_root()`. However, the relevant methods are not exposed yet.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/28089c40c13597bf908802c61352c6fffe0a4465/editor/scene_tree_dock.cpp#L3211-L3214\n\nThe `replacing_by` signal was used in #68599 to automatically set the scene root on change, but this workaround was deprecated in #92760. \n\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2829365607/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833536215","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105669#issuecomment-2833536215","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105669","id":2833536215,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o5FTX","user":{"login":"GrahameGW","id":8879714,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzk3MTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8879714?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW","html_url":"https://github.com/GrahameGW","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-27T16:28:20Z","updated_at":"2025-04-27T16:28:20Z","body":"Does that mean this is more of a `todo!()` situation and less of a \"it's broken\" situation? If I understand these PRs, the old signal was abandoned in favor of a more direct approach, but there's still a bit of work to be done?\n\nIf that's the case, is there a workaround still available or does this require waiting for a new release?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833536215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833687734","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105669#issuecomment-2833687734","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105669","id":2833687734,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o5qS2","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-27T23:15:46Z","updated_at":"2025-04-27T23:56:11Z","body":"If you can operate out of tree (before adding it as an open scene), do so. \n\nIs it necessary to replace the scene root after opening it? Doesn't the SceneTree dock do this job well? \n\nThis is the main reason for deprecating the `replacing_by` signal in #92760.\n\n1. If you can decide on the new configured node before opening the scene, the current editor interface functionality may be sufficient.\n2. **Change Type..** is also a replace operation. If you just want to replace the root node with a **new** unconfigured one, this might be what you need.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833687734/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833751563","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105669#issuecomment-2833751563","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105669","id":2833751563,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o554L","user":{"login":"GrahameGW","id":8879714,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzk3MTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8879714?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW","html_url":"https://github.com/GrahameGW","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-28T00:59:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-28T00:59:10Z","body":"To be perfectly honest, the actual proper way to do what I want to do is probably to use an EditorPostImport script; as I understand the docs that would allow me to assign the root node and set up the pipeline I want to at the time of importing an external file. I wrote my addon before I realized that those were a thing though, so rather than redo it I'm going to just leave it for the time being.\n\nI am not blocked on the project because of this (as you point out, I can just change the node manually), its just a bit more ergonomic if I can use this addon to set the root node type as part of the configuration flow. The idea is that you set a bunch of data via the addon dock (with some gizmos/mesh visualizers to help you), and then save it into a resource, packing the edited scene into it so it can be instantiated later by whatever is referencing the new resource. Allowing the addon to change the root node to the target type (in my case `Structure : StaticBody3D`) would save a step and eliminate a source of error for designers configuring new resources.\n\nRE Change Type doesn't have an accessible API right? It is something only accessible via the editor dropdown? That will continue to work, it just doesn't save the user that extra step.\n\nI'm not sure what that entails for this issue; it sounds like the answer is that the API exists but is just not visible? So perhaps if that isn't scheduled to change soon a PR with some clarification for `replace_by()` is in order? Happy to do it myself if that's what's needed here.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833751563/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833817889","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105669#issuecomment-2833817889","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105669","id":2833817889,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o6KEh","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-28T02:13:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-28T02:43:16Z","body":"```gdscript\n\n...\n\nvar replaced_root := false\nvar scene_path := \"res://addons/replacebygd/GDTestsScene.tscn\"\nvar tmp_path := \"res://tmp.tscn\"\n\n...\n\nfunc on_load_pressed():\n\t#EditorInterface.open_scene_from_path(scene_path)\n\t#root = EditorInterface.get_edited_scene_root()\n\n\t# Open it after the root configuration is completed and replaced.\n\tvar scene : PackedScene = load(scene_path)\n\troot = scene.instantiate()\n\tfirstChild = root.get_child(0)\n\tsecondChild = firstChild.get_child(0)\n\t\n...\n\nfunc replace_root_test():\n\t# Configure the replacement node.\n\tvar replacement = Node3D.new()\n\treplacement.name = \"Replacement\"\n\troot.replace_by(replacement)\n\troot.queue_free()\n\troot = replacement\n\treplaced_root = true\n\n\t# Pack and save as tmp scene.\n\tvar scene = PackedScene.new()\n\n\tvar result = scene.pack(root)\n\tif result == OK:\n\t\tvar error = ResourceSaver.save(scene, tmp_path)  # Or overwrite the original path.\n\t\tif error != OK:\n\t\t\tpush_error(\"An error occurred while saving the scene to disk.\")\n\n\troot.queue_free()\n\t\t\t\n...\n\nfunc _on_open_pressed() -> void:\n\t# Open the (tmp) scene.\n\tEditorInterface.open_scene_from_path(tmp_path if replaced_root else scene_path )\n\treplaced_root = false\n\n\troot = EditorInterface.get_edited_scene_root()\n\tfirstChild = root.get_child(0)\n\tsecondChild = firstChild.get_child(0)\n\n\tpass # Replace with function body.\n```\n\nWhat I mean is that the step of replacing the scene root can be done when the scene is not open. The script can keep some cache data, so it is feasible to save it as a temporary scene and open it for editing. \n\nAutomation configuration and replacement can be done without opening the scene in the editor if inspection and interaction is not required.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833817889/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2908064997","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105669#issuecomment-2908064997","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105669","id":2908064997,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tVYzl","user":{"login":"GrahameGW","id":8879714,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Nzk3MTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8879714?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW","html_url":"https://github.com/GrahameGW","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GrahameGW/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-25T20:30:27Z","updated_at":"2025-05-25T20:30:27Z","body":"Don't know how I missed the response, but that's pretty good. Perhaps I can handle this when closing the scene or before I open it. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2908064997/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]